    {
      "ts": "2026-02-16T08:05:36.160547883-08:00",
      "seq": 234,
      "message": "Alright, let&#39;s talk about this turn! I&#39;m casting my first threat - a 5/5 Eddymurk Crab for 7 mana. Notice I waited until postcombat main to deploy it. Why? Because if my opponent had tried to do something on their turn or during combat, I wanted to keep mana up for interaction like Spell Snare or Burst Lightning. Now that we&#39;re safely in my main phase, I can tap out for my threat while still representing interaction next turn.",
      "type": "chat",
      "from": "Sonnet Teach",
    },
    {
      "ts": "2026-02-16T08:05:46.979485534-08:00",
      "seq": 235,
      "message": "Sonnet Teach puts Eddymurk Crab from stack onto the Battlefield",
    },
    {
      "ts": "2026-02-16T08:05:52.332149976-08:00",
      "seq": 237,
      "message": "Sonnet Teach - Ability triggers: Eddymurk Crab - When Eddymurk Crab enters, tap up to two target creatures.",
