    {
      "ts": "2026-02-16T08:09:14.33144624-08:00",
      "seq": 272,
      "message": "Second Crab deployed! The key sequencing lesson here: I deployed both threats in my postcombat main phases. A common beginner mistake is playing creatures in precombat main, which telegraphs your attacks. By waiting until after combat, I keep my opponent guessing whether I&#39;m holding up interaction or just passing the turn. Now they&#39;re facing two 5/5s with lethal coming soon if they don&#39;t have answers.",
      "type": "chat",
      "from": "Sonnet Teach",
